OL,3,GNEWSACouncil seeks to cut              
OL,4,A'non-essential' translations           
OL,6,FA council has proposed cutting what it 
OL,7,Fcalls "non-essential" translation and  
OL,8,Finterpretation services.               
OL,10,FSunderland City Council's Reform UK    
OL,11,Fleadership revealed the authority spent
OL,12,F#17,680 on the service last year, which
OL,13,Fincluded sign language and braille     
OL,14,Ftranslations that would be protected   
OL,15,Ffrom any changes.                      
OL,17,FCritics say the savings available could
OL,18,Flead to greater costs if people do not 
OL,19,Funderstand such things as tax or       
OL,20,Fregistering children, while others have
OL,21,Fwarned the move may breach equality    
OL,22,Flaws.                                  
OL,23,APub: 27-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
